Description: GtkGLArea: stereo, one view per eye, on a surface of its own, with its depth and colour state
 GtkGLArea gains the API of the edition's GTK 4 stereo area: the property
 stereo, the render signal emitted once for each view (left first) with
 gtk_gl_area_get_current_eye(), stereo-shown and stereo-error, the views'
 own size (stereo-view-width, stereo-view-height), the framebuffer's format
 and the colour state of its values.
 .
 GTK 3 draws a window through one 8 bit buffer, so a stereo area hands its
 picture to the compositor on a surface of its own: the two views copied side
 by side, left first, each at the size it was rendered at, declared as full
 side by side stereo content through libstereo-declare (loaded when the first
 area asks). On Wayland a subsurface placed below the window's surface, sized
 to one view with wp_viewporter, its buffer a dma-buf exported from the area's
 own context in the area's depth (XB24, XB30, XB48, XB4H) and its colour
 described with wp_color_management_v1. On X11 a child window of the toplevel,
 drawn with the area's own GLX context or, on a software renderer, through
 memory (GDK_X11_STEREO_READBACK chooses), placed below the window when the
 window has an alpha channel. The window keeps a transparent hole over the
 area, out of its opaque region, so its widgets drawn over the area stay over
 it.
 .
 An area that cannot be shown per eye says why, once, and renders its left
 view alone until stereo is asked again. An area without stereo is unchanged.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: other, Sparky Stereo OS
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-26
