+ * ## Stereo ##
+ *
+ * An area that asks for stereo (#GtkGLArea:stereo) emits the
+ * #GtkGLArea::render signal twice for each frame, the left view first, and
+ * gtk_gl_area_get_current_eye() tells the handler which view it draws. GTK
+ * copies the two views side by side, left first, into one picture, each at
+ * the size it was rendered at (#GtkGLArea:stereo-view-width), and hands it
+ * to the compositor on a surface of its own, declared as full side by side
+ * stereo content: a subsurface below the window on Wayland, a child window
+ * on X11. The window keeps a transparent hole there, so its widgets drawn
+ * over the area stay over it. The picture keeps the area's depth
+ * (#GtkGLArea:format) and its colour state (#GtkGLArea:color-state) is
+ * described to the compositor with it.
+ *
+ * An area that cannot be shown per eye says why (#GtkGLArea:stereo-error),
+ * logs it once and shows its left view alone, until stereo is asked again.
+ *
  * In order to draw, you have to connect to the #GtkGLArea::render signal,
  * or subclass #GtkGLArea and override the @GtkGLAreaClass.render() virtual
  * function.
